## Description
This example will create another volume bar on the controlBar
```
const player = videojs('myplayer', {
  controlBar: {
    VolumePanel: {
      inline: false
    }
  }
});
```

This example will do what is expected
```
const player = videojs('myplayer', {
  controlBar: {
    volumePanel: {
      inline: false
    }
  }
});
```

This is due to the fact that we use `volumePanel` internally in [`ControlBar.prototype.options_`](https://github.com/videojs/video.js/blob/master/src/js/control-bar/control-bar.js#L59) and because we [`mergeOptions` in `Component`](https://github.com/videojs/video.js/blob/master/src/js/component.js#L65) without doing anything to check case.

The `evented` `one` function only triggers one time with multiple listener, when the mixin object is not targeting itself. 

Evented Mixin on self
```js
let triggered = 0;
let el = new Component();

const listener = () => triggered++;
el.one(['a', 'b'], listener);

el.trigger('a');
// triggered is 1
el.trigger('b');
// triggered is 2
```
Evented Mixin on other
```js
let triggered = 0;
let el = new Component();
let el2 = new Component();
el.one(el2, ['a', 'b'], listener);

el2.trigger('a');
// triggered is 1
el2.trigger('b');
// triggered is still 1
```

* The issue is is due to a [`this.off` call](https://github.com/videojs/video.js/blob/master/src/js/mixins/evented.js#L276) that removes all of the event listeners rather than just the one that triggered the listener.
* This issue wasn't caught because a [test is incorrect](https://github.com/videojs/video.js/blob/master/test/unit/mixins/evented.test.js#L249)

