## Description
608 caption cues do not resize when player is resized.
```
    function shouldCompute(cues) {
      for (var i = 0; i < cues.length; i++) {
        if (cues[i].hasBeenReset || !cues[i].displayState) {
          return true;
        }
      }
      return false;
    } 
    // We don't need to recompute the cues' display states. Just reuse them.
    if (!shouldCompute(cues)) {
      for (var i = 0; i < cues.length; i++) {
        paddedOverlay.appendChild(cues[i].displayState);
      }
      return;
    }
```
In `processCues` from vtt
The issue is a result of `shouldCompute` returning false. Because the cue is already displayed, and it has not been reset.

## Steps to reproduce
Load an HLS playlist with 608 captions.
Select the 608 caption track.
Pause the video while a cue is being displayed.
Set `player.height(200)`. (Or something different than the original)

## Results
### Expected
The cue resizes along with the player.

### Actual
The player resizes, but the captions get left behind.

## Workaround
Set `track.activeCues[0].hasBeenReset = true` right before the resize gets fired for video.js. Where `track` is the displayed text track from the `player.textTracks()` list.

